id: 49264ff6-a958-4f11-a364-ea0ca02bb68f
status: stable
description: Rule detects certain registry patterns associated with Remcos, a type of malware that attackers use to remotely control infected machines.
references:
    - https://any.run/cybersecurity-blog/phishing-google-drive-remcos/
    - https://cert.gov.ua/article/6276824
    - https://cert.gov.ua/article/6276652
    - https://cert.gov.ua/article/6276567
    - https://cert.gov.ua/article/3931296
    - https://cert.gov.ua/article/6276351
    - https://www.jaiminton.com/reverse-engineering/remcos#decrypting-the-remcos-rat-configuration-resource
    - https://any.run/report/51328203fdc519d456202189112621a225491d5acd9af162cf51fa98e898ba00/4d952e56-e562-4d3b-82d2-0842823555d0
    - https://www.uptycs.com/blog/remcos-rat-uac-0500-pipe-method
    - https://www.trellix.com/blogs/research/unmasking-the-hidden-threat-inside-a-sophisticated-excel-based-attack-delivering-fileless-remcos-rat/
    - https://www.ibm.com/think/x-force/hive0156-continues-remcos-campaigns-against-ukraine
    - https://www.seqrite.com/blog/deceptive-layoff-themed-hr-email-distributes-remcos-rat-malware/
    - https://asec.ahnlab.com/en/92160/
author: SOC Prime Team
tags:
    - attack.persistence
    - attack.t1547.001
logsource:
    product: windows
    category: registry_event
detection:
    selection_base:
        TargetObject|contains:
            - '\Software' #\HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\Rmc-4E12ZU; https://www.seqrite.com/blog/deceptive-layoff-themed-hr-email-distributes-remcos-rat-malware/
            - '\CurrentVersion'
    selection_vars:
        TargetObject|contains:
            - '\Remcos'
            - '\Rmc-' #Rmc-LQH1JR
    condition: selection_base and selection_vars
falsepositives:
    - The reliance on the surrounding environment may necessitate the implementation of additional filtering measures to prevent false positives.
level: high
"#,
  // Possible Powershell Executing Process In Suspicious Working Directory (via cmdline)
  "4a73122b-10d6-4465-8cec-c11d616ec1de": r#"title: Possible Powershell Executing Process In Suspicious Working Directory (via cmdline)
id: 4a73122b-10d6-4465-8cec-c11d616ec1de
status: stable
description: Identifies powershell executing process in suspicious working directory, which may be an indicator of malicious activity.
author: SOC Prime Team
references:
    - https://www.seqrite.com/blog/threat-actors-are-targeting-us-tax-session-with-new-tactics-of-stealerium-infostealer/
    - https://www.zscaler.com/blogs/security-research/technical-analysis-marco-stealers
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/02/05/clickfix-variant-crashfix-deploying-python-rat-trojan/
    - https://www.pointwild.com/threat-intelligence/covert-rat-phishing-campaign/
    - https://www.elastic.co/security-labs/silentconnect-delivers-screenconnect
tags:
    - attack.t1059.001
    - attack.execution
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_base:
        Image|endswith: 'powershell.exe'
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'Start' # Start-Process -FilePath revolaomt.exe -WorkingDirectory Senv:TEMP
            - 'Process'
            - 'WorkingDirectory'
    selection_path:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'TEMP' #https://www.elastic.co/security-labs/silentconnect-delivers-screenconnect
            - 'AppData' # https://www.pointwild.com/threat-intelligence/covert-rat-phishing-campaign/
            - 'ProgramData'
            - 'Public'
    condition: selection_base and selection_path
falsepositives:
    - Unknown
level: medium
